current='privacy.html'
body=intro('YOUR INFORMATION','Privacy, in plain language.','How Morocco Explorer Tours handles information when you visit, plan or enquire about a journey.')+'''<section class="container prose collection"><h2>Who we are</h2><p>Morocco Explorer Tours is based in Marrakech, Morocco. For privacy questions or requests, contact <a href="mailto:moroccoexploredtours@gmail.com">moroccoexploredtours@gmail.com</a> or call <a href="tel:+212704321335">+212 704 321 335</a>.</p><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>The trip planner on this website prepares a brief in your browser. It does not send the form to our server, save it in a database or store it in browser storage. Copying or downloading the brief is an action you choose; reloading the page clears the entries. If you contact us by email, phone, WhatsApp or social media, we receive the details you choose to share. When you arrange a booking with us, we may also need travel details such as names, dates, group size, accommodation preferences and special requirements.</p><p>Please do not put passport numbers, payment card details or sensitive medical information in the website trip planner. Payment and booking services you choose may collect information under their own privacy terms.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use enquiry and booking details to respond to you, prepare or manage the travel services you request, coordinate necessary reservations with suppliers, meet legal obligations and handle customer service. We may rely on your request or booking, your consent where needed, legal requirements or our legitimate operational interests, depending on the context.</p><h2>Who may receive information</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. If you ask us to arrange travel, we may share relevant details with hotels, transport providers, guides, activity operators, booking platforms and service providers only as needed to plan or deliver that request. Some providers may operate outside your home country. When you follow a link to WhatsApp, email, social media or another external service, that service handles the information you send under its own terms.</p><h2>Website logs, cookies and analytics</h2><p>This version of the website does not include analytics, advertising trackers, newsletter sign-up or third-party social media widgets. The hosting provider may process standard connection logs, such as an IP address and request time, to deliver and protect the site. Your browser may use its own settings or retain data when you open an external service.</p><h2>Keeping information secure and for how long</h2><p>We use reasonable safeguards for information we handle. We retain enquiry and booking records only for as long as needed to respond, provide the requested services, meet applicable record-keeping duties and resolve disputes.</p><h2>Your requests</h2><p>You may contact us to ask what personal information we hold about you, request a correction or ask us to delete or limit its use. We will consider and respond to your request under the rules that apply; some records may need to be retained for legal or booking-related reasons.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this page when our services or practices change. The current version is the one published here.</p><p><strong>Last updated: 9 October 2026.</strong></p></section>'''
write(current,'Privacy Policy','Read how Morocco Explorer Tours handles website, enquiry and booking information.',body)
current='terms-and-conditions.html'
body=intro('BEFORE YOU TRAVEL','Terms and Conditions','The booking, cancellation and travel conditions for journeys arranged by Morocco Explorer Tours.')+'''<section class="container prose collection"><p>By asking Morocco Explorer Tours to arrange a tour, you accept these conditions for yourself and the other travellers included in your booking. We will confirm the itinerary, price, inclusions and payment instructions in a written proposal or invoice. A booking is confirmed when we receive the required deposit, normally 20% to 30% of the total invoice, as stated in your proposal. Unless your proposal states otherwise, the remaining balance is payable in cash on the day the tour begins.</p><h2>Changes and cancellations</h2><p>If you need to change or cancel a confirmed trip, contact us in writing as soon as possible. We will confirm whether a requested change can be arranged. If it cannot, you may keep the original arrangements or cancel under these terms.</p><ul><li>Cancellation received 30 days or more before the tour starts: the deposit is retained.</li><li>Cancellation received less than 30 days before the tour starts: the full tour price is payable and no refund is available.</li></ul><p>Events beyond reasonable control—including severe weather, natural disasters, civil unrest, airport or road closures, strikes, terrorism or official travel restrictions—may disrupt a trip. We will discuss practical alternatives, but costs already committed to suppliers may not be refundable. Nothing in these conditions removes any rights or responsibilities that cannot legally be excluded.</p><h2>Special requirements and preferences</h2><p>Tell us before confirming if anyone travelling has dietary needs, medical requirements, mobility needs or another condition that may affect the tour. Where needed, we may share the relevant information with the suppliers arranging the service. Tell us about preferences such as hotel location or bed configuration when booking. We will try to accommodate them, but a preference is not guaranteed unless it is confirmed in writing.</p><h2>Transport and itinerary changes</h2><p>Transport arranged for your tour will use vehicles licensed and insured for tourist transport, with passenger capacity appropriate to the group. Routes and activities may need to change because of weather, road conditions, mechanical issues, supplier availability or a driver's or guide's health. The driver or guide may make reasonable operational adjustments for safety and local conditions. Delays can affect onward connections, so we recommend scheduling flights or other onward travel no earlier than the day after your tour ends.</p><h2>Travel insurance</h2><p>All travellers must have suitable travel insurance covering personal belongings, accident or injury, medical expenses and repatriation, including emergency medical transport. Your policy should include at least €5,000 of medical and repatriation cover. We recommend cancellation cover and checking that your policy covers activities you plan to take, including camel or horse riding, trekking, quad biking and travel over rough ground or at altitude.</p><h2>Travel documents</h2><p>You are responsible for carrying a valid passport, any required visa and a confirmed return or onward ticket, and for meeting the entry requirements that apply to your nationality. Morocco Explorer Tours is not responsible for costs caused by missing or invalid travel documents, subject to applicable law.</p><h2>Suppliers and responsibility</h2><p>Some elements of a trip are supplied by independent hotels, carriers, guides or activity operators. We coordinate the services described in your confirmed proposal and will help address problems reported during the trip. We are not responsible for a supplier's actions or for circumstances beyond our reasonable control, except where applicable law makes us responsible.</p><h2>Safety equipment</h2><p>For cycling or other activities, the availability and standard of locally supplied protective equipment can vary. Ask us before booking if you have a specific equipment requirement; you may prefer to bring your own properly fitted equipment.</p><h2>Privacy and photographs</h2><p>We use booking information to arrange the services you request and share relevant details with the suppliers involved. We will ask for your permission before using identifiable photographs or a case study from your trip in public promotional material. See our <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> for details about information handling.</p><h2>Complaints</h2><p>If an issue arises during your tour, tell your driver, guide or accommodation provider promptly so they can try to resolve it. If it remains unresolved, contact us with the details while you are still travelling when possible; this gives us the best opportunity to help.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For booking or terms questions, email <a href="mailto:moroccoexploredtours@gmail.com">moroccoexploredtours@gmail.com</a>, call <a href="tel:+212704321335">+212 704 321 335</a> or message <a href="https://wa.me/212704321335">WhatsApp</a>.</p><p><strong>Last updated: 9 October 2026.</strong></p></section>'''
write(current,'Terms and Conditions','Read the booking, cancellation, travel and safety conditions for tours arranged by Morocco Explorer Tours.',body)
